This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   The user is developing a xiaozhi_voice application on a bes2800 development board running Vela RTOS (NuttX-based). This is a voice assistant that connects to the Xiaozhi cloud service via WebSocket over TLS (wss), enabling real-time voice interaction using Opus audio codec (16kHz mono uplink, 24kHz mono downlink). It also uses MCP (Model Context Protocol) to control local device features like stopwatch and alarms.

   Previous session fixes were: (a) long-press Speak button causing stuck Listening state, (b) build linker error from stale .o files, (c) adding reconnect mechanism to connect_thread.

   **Current bug report**: The user says the first voice input works perfectly (recognizes content, triggers alarm setting via MCP), but when they long-press the Speak button a second time, it shows error and the button goes gray. They provided a detailed serial log.

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Vela RTOS (NuttX-based) on bes2800 development board
   - WebSocket over TLS (wss) using mbedtls for secure communication
   - Opus audio codec: 16kHz mono for uplink (mic capture), 24kHz mono for downlink (TTS playback)
   - LVGL (Light and Versatile Graphics Library) for UI with animations
   - MCP (Model Context Protocol) - JSON-RPC based protocol for AI to invoke device-side tools
   - Multi-threaded architecture: main thread (LVGL), connect_thread, recv_thread, capture_thread, dialog_round_thread
   - State machine: BOOT → OTA → CONNECT → READY → LISTENING → THINKING → PLAYING → DONE → ERROR
   - SMF (Streaming Media Framework) for audio capture (PCM) and playback (Opus decode)
   - cJSON library for JSON parsing/generation
   - BinaryProtocol3 header for Opus uplink frames
   - `volatile bool app_running` lifecycle flag distinguishing connection drops from app deletion
   - Race conditions between LVGL UI thread and worker threads during connection drops
   - TLS error -0x5 = MBEDTLS_ERR_SSL_PEER_CLOSE_NOTIFY (server-initiated close)

3. Files and Code Sections:
   - **xiaozhi_voice/xiaozhi_main.c** (~1800+ lines, central orchestrator)
     - Contains: UI creation, state machine, all thread definitions, MCP tool callbacks, animation code
     - Key structures: `struct xiaozhi_app_s` (app state with ws, audio, UI handles, lifecycle flags)

     **capture_thread (lines 730-772)**: Captures opus frames while `app->capturing && !app->capture_stop && app->ws_connected`. Sets `capturing = false` on exit.
     ```c
     static void *capture_thread(void *arg)
     {
       struct xiaozhi_app_s *app = arg;
       int ret = xiaozhi_audio_start_capture(app->audio);
       app->capture_started = true;
       if (ret != 0) { app->capturing = false; return NULL; }
       printf("[xiaozhi] capture: buffering opus frames\n");
       while (app->capturing && !app->capture_stop && app->ws_connected &&
              app->frame_buf_cnt < XZ_FRAME_BUF_COUNT) {
         ssize_t n = xiaozhi_audio_read_opus(app->audio, ...);
         if (n < 0) break;
         if (n > 0) { app->frame_buf[app->frame_buf_cnt].len = n; app->frame_buf_cnt++; }
       }
       printf("[xiaozhi] capture: buffered %d frames\n", app->frame_buf_cnt);
       app->capturing = false;
       return NULL;
     }
     ```

     **speak_btn_event_cb (lines 1312-1410)**: Button press/release handler. PRESSED creates capture_thread, RELEASED sets capture_stop and creates dialog_round_thread.
     ```c
     static void speak_btn_event_cb(lv_event_t *e)
     {
       struct xiaozhi_app_s *app = &g_app;
       lv_event_code_t code = lv_event_get_code(e);
       if (!app->handshake_done || app->ws_dead) {
         if (app->capturing) {  // cleanup for mid-capture ws_dead
           app->capturing = false;
           app->capture_stop = true;
           pthread_mutex_lock(&s_ui_mutex);
           app->state = XZ_STATE_ERROR;
           pthread_mutex_unlock(&s_ui_mutex);
         }
         return;  // <-- KEY: returns early if handshake_done=false
       }
       if (app->dialog_running) return;
       if (code == LV_EVENT_PRESSED) {
         app->capturing = true;
         app->capture_stop = false;
         app->frame_buf_cnt = 0;
         pthread_mutex_lock(&s_ui_mutex);
         app->state = XZ_STATE_LISTENING;
         pthread_mutex_unlock(&s_ui_mutex);
         pthread_create(&app->capture_tid, &attr, capture_thread, app);
         app->capture_tid_valid = true;
       } else if (code == LV_EVENT_RELEASED) {
         if (!app->capturing) return;  // <-- If capturing was cleared by cleanup, returns early!
         app->capture_stop = true;
         app->capturing = false;
         app->dialog_running = true;
         pthread_mutex_lock(&s_ui_mutex);
         app->state = XZ_STATE_THINKING;
         pthread_mutex_unlock(&s_ui_mutex);
         pthread_create(NULL, &attr, dialog_round_thread, app);
       }
     }
     ```

     **dialog_round_thread (lines 1182-1305)**: Joins capture thread, runs validity check, sends audio to server, waits for STT/TTS. Clears frame_buf_cnt and dialog_running at end.
     ```c
     static void *dialog_round_thread(void *arg)
     {
       // Signal capture to stop, join it
       app->capture_stop = true; app->capturing = false;
       while (!app->capture_started && spin < 3000) usleep(10000);
       xiaozhi_audio_stop_capture(app->audio);
       pthread_join(app->capture_tid, NULL);
       // Validity check, then send listen:start, drain, listen:stop
       // Wait for STT + TTS
       while (!app->tts_playing && app->ws_connected && waited < 15000) usleep(100000);
       while (app->tts_playing && app->ws_connected) usleep(100000);
     back_to_ready:
       if (app->ws_connected) app->state = XZ_STATE_READY;
       else app->state = XZ_STATE_ERROR;
       app->capturing = false; app->capture_stop = false;
       app->got_stt = false; app->frame_buf_cnt = 0;
       app->dialog_running = false;
       return NULL;
     }
     ```

     **recv_thread (lines 818-937)**: Background receive thread. On error, sets ws_connected=false, ws_dead=true and exits.
     ```c
     static void *recv_thread(void *arg)
     {
       while (app->ws_connected) {
         ret = xiaozhi_ws_recv(&app->ws, &payload, &plen, &is_binary);
         if (ret != 0) {
           app->ws_connected = false;
           app->ws_dead = true;
           break;
         }
         // Parse STT, TTS, LLM, MCP messages...
       }
     }
     ```

